{
	title: 'Tool prompt guides live in their tool modules',
	spec: "Each tool's prompt guide (when and how to use it, with examples) lives in its module beside its syntax, not in SYSTEM.md. Guides use SYSTEM.md's template language, so they keep conditions such as $session_interactive and variables such as $session_id. SYSTEM.md places guide sections generated from the tool registry, replacing its hand-written READ, GREP, BASH, EDIT and Compaction sections; general rules stay in SYSTEM.md. Each guide teaches only the canonical form, with blocks for multi-line or quoted arguments (task 0nt); leniency stays unadvertised (task hq6). Tools without a prompt guide keep their one-line summary in Other tools, and HELP <TOOL> remains their detailed syntax. Rendering stays byte-identical across requests for prompt caching; a guide change reaches running sessions as a section update (task vd9). Plugins can add or replace a tool's guide.",
	status: 'planned',
	notes: [
		'Open, 2026-11-19: which tools get a full guide in the prompt and which only a one-line summary plus HELP. Decide when implementing; ask the user if unclear.',
		"From 10-cfg, 2026-11-19: when moving guides, drop 'then' from EDIT's 'replace A-B then !!NEW, new lines, !!END' (models write 'then !!NEW' literally); WAIT takes { timeout: <seconds> }, so BASH's 'set timeout and use WAIT' line applies to both.",
		'Decided 2026-11-19 (user): a tool module starts with its why-comment and imports, then summary, help (starting with "## <TOOL>", prose at column 0; guides are subsections of # Tools), parameters without field descriptions, syntax, run, helpers, and a short export. inPrompt tools (BASH, EDIT, GREP, READ) appear in full via $tools; every other tool with a summary gets one Other tools line; HELP has none because the Tools section names it. Short arguments (READ paths, GREP patterns, NOTIFY text, BRAVE queries, COMMAND) stay quoted.',
		'Lesson: the running host renders SYSTEM.md with its loaded guides(); a new SYSTEM.md before a host restart reports sections cannot nest. Inside EDIT blocks, a help text line that is exactly !!END must be written !!!END.',
		'Decided 2026-11-19 (user): every tool module declares const inPrompt (true or false) as configuration, under one comment telling humans what each value does. Tool.promptIf holds a template condition guides() wraps around the tool section or Other tools line; SPAWN uses $spawn_budget. guides() omits the Other tools heading when no other tool remains.',
		"Fixed 2026-11-25: EDIT's HELP usage no longer calls EDIT an exception; BASH, EVAL, SEND, SPAWN and COMPACT also take raw lines in blocks now.",
		"Changed 2026-11-25 (user): Tool.promptIf became enableIf. tools.allowed() evaluates it with the session's prompt variables (systemPrompt.holds), so a false condition removes the tool from the prompt, HELP and calls alike."
	],
	needs: ['0nt', 'hq6'],
	foldInto: ['vd9']
}
